{
  "requirement": "For requirement and example evidence, both `true` and `FIXME` MUST satisfy the determination check in `habeas::validate()`. A false determination MUST fail validation and be reported with its rationale. Each definition's determination MUST be checked on its own; a false determination MUST NOT fail the definitions it implements, tests, or cites. All other evidence checks MUST still pass: FIXME MUST NOT excuse malformed, missing, or stale evidence or uncovered references. Validation MUST check the recorded outcome, schema, input freshness, and reference coverage without inference or reassessing whether a source comment adequately acknowledges a gap.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no gaps. The code, markings and tests cover every obligation in `requirements.ci.determination`.\n\n**Obligations and the code that carries them out**\n- **True and FIXME satisfy the determination check.** In `validate_evidence_file` (`src/evidence.rs`), `Judgment::from_value` parses the `determination` field. Only `Judgment::False` adds a determination error, so `true` and FIXME add none. The only other check on a FIXME entry is that it parses.\n- **A false determination fails validation and is reported with its rationale.** The block marked `{impl}requirements.ci.determination` pushes `\"{label}: determination is false: <trimmed rationale>\"` into `errors`. `habeas::validate()` (`src/lib.rs`) panics on any non-empty `errors`, so the record fails validation.\n- **Each definition is checked on its own, and a false determination does not fail the definitions it implements, tests or cites.** The false error is built only from that record's own label. `validate_references` never consults another record's determination. The only determination-dependent condition there is the \"true example without `{test}`\" check, which is the example's own and is covered by `requirements.examples.evidence`.\n- **FIXME does not excuse malformed, missing, stale or uncovered evidence.** Schema checks, text checks, input freshness (`validate_input`) and reference coverage (`validate_references`: \"no input covers\", \"reference set changed\", anchors) all run regardless of the determination. The `true` versus FIXME distinction affects only the example-without-`{test}` check. That is the intended exemption, specified by `requirements.ci.fixme_example_test_gaps`, which the test below marks.\n- **Validation checks the recorded outcome without inference or reassessing comments.** The code only reads the recorded `determination` value. It never inspects source comments to decide whether they acknowledge a gap.\n- **Unmarked or extra behavior.** `src/citations.rs` `fn[validate]` also carries an `{impl}` for this requirement, but that falls outside \"requirement and example evidence\". It is an over-marking, not a gap.\n- **No unmarked implementing code.** Beyond the sources the references tool reports and the false-determination handling in `validate_review` for citation reviews (which is outside this requirement's scope), I found none.\n\n**Tests**\n- `a_false_determination_fails_only_its_own_record_with_its_rationale` (`src/evidence.rs`) asserts three things:\n  - The exact error text includes the trimmed rationale.\n  - It is the only error.\n  - A requirement that is both implemented and cited by the false one is unaffected.\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` asserts that \"determination is false\" is reported alongside the other errors.\n- `fixme_requirements_accept_issue_references_and_other_content` and `fixme_fixture` (`tests/outcomes.rs`, `tests/commands.rs`) show FIXME records, both with and without issue numbers, validating with no errors.\n- `fixme_examples_pass_without_test_references_but_true_examples_do_not` shows a FIXME example needs no `{test}` reference, a `true` one does, and a false one reports \"determination is false\".\n- `fixme_does_not_hide_stale_inputs_or_uncovered_references` shows a FIXME record still fails on a stale input and on an uncovered reference.\n- The two `tests/authoring_batch.rs` tests exercise determinations end to end. They show true, FIXME and false records validating or failing as expected.\n\nAll obligations have `{impl}` markings and tests.",
  "references": "7654bcb6b2ec344e3bb41e2d6842db9ad15628cf9a7e6b60a146d2ee61372222",
